{
  "name": "coincidence_audit",
  "task": "Deliver a two-file radio observatory coverage audit. Input x has 'window':[lo,hi], 'quorum' (positive integer) and 'records':[[instrument,start,end],...]. Records are half-open intervals, may repeat or overlap for the same instrument, and may extend beyond the window. Count DISTINCT instruments observing at the same time after clipping to [lo,hi). Produce every maximal interval where the count is at least quorum. Merge touching qualified spans even when the participating instruments change. Discard empty intervals. Return a dict mapping 'coverage.csv' and 'audit.json' to their file texts. CSV starts start,end with a final newline; rows sorted by start. Audit JSON must have keys 'covered' (total qualifying length) and 'longest' ([start,end] of the longest qualifying interval, earliest on ties, or null). Up to 60,000 records; coordinates can be trillions apart. Do not iterate over the time axis.",
  "compare": {
    "coverage.csv": "csv",
    "audit.json": "json"
  },
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": {
        "window": [
          0,
          12
        ],
        "quorum": 2,
        "records": [
          [
            "A",
            0,
            5
          ],
          [
            "A",
            2,
            7
          ],
          [
            "B",
            3,
            6
          ],
          [
            "C",
            6,
            10
          ]
        ]
      },
      "output": {
        "coverage.csv": "start,end\n3,7\n",
        "audit.json": "{\"covered\": 4, \"longest\": [3, 7]}"
      }
    },
    {
      "input": {
